# Releases no update may skip. A panel behind one installs it first, and the newest release on its
# next update, so each step runs the installer the step before it placed (install.sh
# _apply_update_stop; the Update card offers the same commit, system_ops._update_stop).
#
# Add a release here when the NEXT release depends on something it teaches the installed updater,
# the recovery command or the helper, which run from root-owned copies a release replaces only once
# it is installed. One line per release: its full commit id on main, then why.
#
# The entry goes in WITH the release that depends on it (a commit cannot name its own id, and the
# list is read from the commit an update would install, after that commit's signature is checked):
# an update to a target that does not list the stop skips it. The stop must be a signed release whose
# checks passed, or panels behind it are offered nothing until it is.
#
# Only an updater that has this feature follows the list: a panel on an older release goes straight
# to the newest one, as before. The first entry is older than this feature, so it takes effect only
# when a newer installer runs over an older checkout (a hand run, the deploy).
